# Security headers (issue #144, F-SEC-003).
#
# This file follows the `_headers` convention honored by Netlify and
# Cloudflare Pages. The site currently deploys to GitHub Pages, which does
# not support custom response headers — GH Pages serves this file verbatim
# as a static asset instead. On GitHub Pages the enforceable equivalents
# live in `src/components/SecurityHeaders.astro` (meta CSP + referrer meta),
# rendered into every page head by both layouts. `frame-ancestors` and
# `X-Frame-Options` cannot be expressed via meta tags, so this file is the
# only place clickjacking protection is declared; it activates automatically
# if the site ever moves to a host that honors `_headers`. Keep the CSP
# directives below in sync with the meta CSP in SecurityHeaders.astro —
# the only intentional difference is `frame-ancestors` (headers-only).

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
